                "word": "archéoptéryx",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c9197908-6a93-3261-9277-d671cfab2d54",
                        "entry_id": "329beb0c-1d6b-34d9-a782-2d143604773f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Oiseau fossile qui est le plus ancien que nous connaissons."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "86d65d44-a035-4885-9630-eae8e598e963",
                                "sense_id": "c9197908-6a93-3261-9277-d671cfab2d54",
                                "text": "Ces êtres paradoxaux étaient dignes de leurs émules, les reptiles nageurs (ichtyosaures, plésiosaures, téléosaures, mosasaures, hyléosaures, etc.) ou des reptiles volants, tels que le ptérodactyle qui partageaient le royaume des airs avec l’archéoptéryx, le premier oiseau (ce dernier était de petite taille)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e79132d7-6e19-4438-b3b9-263e6bf6d493",
                                "sense_id": "c9197908-6a93-3261-9277-d671cfab2d54",
                                "text": "Les ptérodactyles de Raoul prennent une allure plus effilée et ressemblent à des archéoptéryx."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ffd04df9-5e95-4d61-a68e-3c1edf2ab8fb",
                        "source_entry_id": "329beb0c-1d6b-34d9-a782-2d143604773f",
                        "source_sense_id": "c9197908-6a93-3261-9277-d671cfab2d54",
                        "target_lang_word": "archeopteryx",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "archeopteryx",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "131c005e-8748-37be-92cb-59d50618c098",
                                        "entry_id": "6974d882-0926-35ee-a228-6d6f3a442128",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A specimen of the species Archaeopteryx lithographica, being the earliest and most primitive known bird, representing a transition in the evolution of dinosaurs to birds."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e534a30e-bf39-416b-bc9a-4516727288d2",
                                                "sense_id": "131c005e-8748-37be-92cb-59d50618c098",
                                                "text": "Since Pterosaurians are triassic and the Archæopteryges jurassic we are justified in regarding the actual chronology of external integument in the geological strata as : first, scale ; second, hair ; and third, feather. This inspires us to make a wider appeal to geology in order to have a comprehensive sketch of the avian sequence."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
